Subject: [PATCH] X11: preserve the requested target when a clipboard read fails

A clipboard callback may return NULL when a remote format cannot be
retrieved or converted. Keep the requested target in SelectionNotify even
on failure; property=None is the failure indicator. Mutter matches replies
by selection and target before checking property, so target=None leaves
the Wayland reader waiting indefinitely.

Reproduced with SDL 3.2.30 on GNOME Wayland using a callback that advertises
text/html and returns NULL. wl-paste times out without this change and
receives an empty response with it.

Upstream: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/16568
Tracking: https://github.com/shakeelosmani/avd_feed_connect/issues/49
Remove this patch when the pinned SDL release includes the upstream fix.

diff --git a/src/video/x11/SDL_x11events.c b/src/video/x11/SDL_x11events.c
--- a/src/video/x11/SDL_x11events.c
+++ b/src/video/x11/SDL_x11events.c
@@ -707,7 +707,7 @@
         SDL_zero(sevent);
         sevent.xany.type = SelectionNotify;
         sevent.xselection.selection = req->selection;
-        sevent.xselection.target = None;
+        sevent.xselection.target = req->target;
         sevent.xselection.property = None; // tell them no by default
         sevent.xselection.requestor = req->requestor;
         sevent.xselection.time = req->time;
